e escaped they use the  humanitarian corridor and the uh  and it was possible to escape because  the season fire held for some time but  then shelling began again i think it  would be very difficult to get out of  the city without any uh corridor without  any agreement right now because the city  is completely surrounded and fighting  has been going on around the around the  city now the situation in there is dire  it's been more than 10 days that people  have had no food no water no medicine no  electricity we also have spa  scarce information from there because uh  mostly the phones are down or the  the mobile network so uh it's a it's a  very dire situation and we're hearing  that thousands have died already  and in kiev matthias where you are we  understand there have been more  explosions near the center can you tell  us more about what's happening there  yeah there were several explosions at  night some of them quite loud we heard  them here and uh it seems that again  residential buildings have been hit uh a  ten-story building was on fire and  another nine-story building has been hit  also on the north in the northern part  of the city and it seems that russia is  intensifying it's uh it's shelling off  the city and its bombings of the city uh  in the sky has been  had had been spared we have to say for  some time of heavy uh bombings after  initial initially some uh bombs if you  remember the tv tower bomb hit the hit  the city but uh then it was a bit calmer  and now this has  resumed and  we have visited one of these buildings  these residential buildings that have  been hit by a shell yesterday  yaroslav nafilloninka has been sitting  outside her apartment since the early  morning hours she's waiting for someone  to pick her up after the apartment she  has been living for decades was shelled  overnight  this is it  one room another small one and a kitchen  that's what it was  it was 5 am when a shell hit the house  there was a loud bang  and then immedia